 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- Precision: Logarithms in $\mathcal{L}_{\text{sparse}}$ can cause numerical issues if $\alpha_i$ is 0 or 1. Clamping $\alpha_i$ to $[\epsilon, 1-\epsilon]$ is recommended [G].
-- Boundaries: Points near the edge of the pixel area may be inconsistently included/excluded. Consistent pixel-point intersection testing is required [G].
-- Degenerate Input: If fewer than $k$ points intersect a pixel, the buffer is filled with fewer points, and $T_i$ computation adjusts accordingly [S1].
